@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@token = techhive-secret-token

### Public: root and health check (no token needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Authentication: no token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### Authentication: wrong token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer wrong-token

### List all users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List users filtered by department, with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users?department=IT&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get a user by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get a user that does not exist -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a user -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Can",
  "lastName": "Ozturk",
  "email": "can.ozturk@techhive.com",
  "department": "Finance",
  "jobTitle": "Accountant"
}

### Create a user with invalid data -> 400 with field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "X",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "department": "",
  "jobTitle": ""
}

### Create a user with an existing email -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ayse",
  "lastName": "Yilmaz",
  "email": "ayse.yilmaz@techhive.com",
  "department": "HR",
  "jobTitle": "HR Manager"
}

### Update a user -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ayse",
  "lastName": "Yilmaz",
  "email": "ayse.yilmaz@techhive.com",
  "department": "HR",
  "jobTitle": "Head of HR"
}

### Delete a user -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/3
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Trigger an unhandled exception -> 500 JSON error from the error-handling middleware
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test-error
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
